    {
      "id": "f9a6rwb",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Period</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Hindi Name</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Approximate Time</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Features / Representative Works</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Adikal / Veer Gaatha Kaal</p>",
            "<p>आदिकाल / वीरगाथा काल</p>",
            "<p>700 CE – 1400 CE</p>",
            "<p>Heroic poems glorifying warriors and kings; Prithviraaj Raso (Chandbardai); Alha-Udal; oral tradition; Apabhramsha and early Hindi</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bhakti Kaal (Medieval-I)</p>",
            "<p>भक्तिकाल</p>",
            "<p>1400 CE – 1700 CE</p>",
            "<p>Golden age; devotional poetry; Nirguna (Kabir, Nanak, Dadu) and Saguna (Surdas, Tulsidas, Mira); mysticism, social reform; Ramcharitmanas, Sursagar, Bijak</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Riti Kaal (Medieval-II)</p>",
            "<p>रीतिकाल</p>",
            "<p>1600 CE – 1850 CE</p>",
            "<p>Court poetry; elaborate rhetoric (alankar); Sringara rasa dominant; Keshavdas (Rasikpriya), Bihari (Satsai), Bhushan (Shivabhushana :veer rasa exception)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Adhunik Kaal / Khariboli Kaal</p>",
            "<p>आधुनिक काल</p>",
            "<p>1850 CE – Present</p>",
            "<p>Modern Hindi; prose and poetry in Khariboli Hindi; 4 sub-periods: Bhartendu (1850-1900), Dwivedi (1900-1920), Chhayavad (1920-1936), Pragativad/Prayogvad/Nayi Kavita onwards</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "w5da3xs",
